# Citation metadata (https://citation-file-format.github.io/). GitHub renders
# it as the repository's "Cite this repository" box and Zenodo reads it when
# minting a release DOI. `version` must equal pyproject.toml's -- the
# version-consistency test enforces it, and scripts/bump_version.py rewrites
# both `version` and `date-released` on every bump. When Zenodo has minted a
# concept DOI for the repository, add it here as
#   identifiers:
#     - type: doi
#       value: 10.5281/zenodo.XXXXXXX
#       description: Concept DOI for all versions
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata from this file.
type: software
title: "SageMath MCP Server"
abstract: >-
  A Model Context Protocol server that gives a language model a sandboxed
  mathematical subset of SageMath: 40 stateful tools for symbolic calculus,
  algebra, number theory, graphs, groups, elliptic curves, plotting and claim
  verification, with a persistent Sage session per client, a deny-by-default
  AST policy in front of it and a hardened container as the real boundary.
authors:
  - family-names: Steinl
    given-names: Christoph
    affiliation: XBP Europe
  - name: XBP Europe
    website: https://github.com/XBP-Europe
version: 0.7.0
date-released: 2026-09-07
license: MIT
repository-code: https://github.com/XBP-Europe/sagemath-mcp
repository-artifact: https://pypi.org/project/sagemath-mcp/
url: https://github.com/XBP-Europe/sagemath-mcp#readme
keywords:
  - SageMath
  - Model Context Protocol
  - MCP
  - computer algebra
  - symbolic computation
  - large language models
  - tool use
  - sandboxing
references:
  - type: software
    title: SageMath, the Sage Mathematics Software System
    authors:
      - name: The Sage Developers
    url: https://www.sagemath.org
    notes: >-
      The computation runtime this server drives. It is GPL-2.0-or-later and
      is used as a separate process; no SageMath source is redistributed here.
